			"text": "Caeruleum was a jawless fish discovered in Jiufotang Formation of China, dating back to the Early Cretaceous. Caeruleum, not to be confused with Caeruleum (paint) and Caeruleum (lichen), is a Lamprey named after Caeuleum (paint) which was a blue paint used in Ancient Egypt. The type species, C. miraculum, was comparable to extant species of lamprey, growing to around 24 to 42 centimeters."
